And the Ducks' shutout search will last yet another game, as Kyle Connor slips behind the Ducks defense to put one up top. Jets' first shot of the period.

Anaheim has now gone 167 games without a shutout. Its last clean sheet came in the 2024-25 season opener.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Don't let this Ducks fourth line get out and running!

Washe with an excellent strip back in the D zone, and its off to the races. Caulfield with a great pass to get Malott going, who feeds Washe to double the Ducks' lead.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Edmonton now up by three with a 5-goal second period. Connor McDavid picks up speed at 4-on-4 just rips a wrist shot that leaks through Lukáš Dostál.

5-3 Oilers. What a turnaround.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Edmonton takes the lead. Anaheim simply unable to clear the puck cleanly, and at the end of a very, very long shift, a lot of straight-legged defense as Evan Bouchard scores his second.

3-2 Oilers. 5:48 P2.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Beckett Sennecke, YOU are the 🎶 Dancing Queen 🎶 

Ducks power play stays red hot. 1-0 over Edmonton.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ladies and gentlemen, the Anaheim Ducks may just have a power play, and its trigger man is Cutter Gauthier.

His second of the game, but look at this puck movement. LaCombe, Carlsson, Sennecke. 2-1 Ducks.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Florida equalizes on a bit of a lax play from everyone behind/around the net.

Slow flip from Dostál, slow decision from LaCombe, Washe sends behind for the turnover, Dostál can't get quite corral it in the chaos around the crease. 1-1.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether
